\f0\b \cf2 Whose eyes, and the tone
\f1\b0 \
Chanta's scene, close in on him. (canon) Deadpan and self-mocking on top \'97 the Blow Shit Up Lounge, the fireworks, his own flatness with his mates \'97 with real loss underneath: his old world slipping away. [mine \'97 the tone read, from chanta.md and your steer] Leave room for the rhythm.\

\f0\b Setting
\f1\b0 \
The Blow Shit Up Lounge \'97 the rebuilt Stickett Inn (the old bomb site), fireworks going off daily. (your steer; canon: timeline, "Hayley Investigates the Stickett Inn") He's got something to write on and a drink; the fireworks keep cutting across it. [mine \'97 props] Time: a few weeks before the concert (Sat 10 Nov). No year.\

\f0\b Who's there and what they know
\f1\b0 \
Chanta; Abe and Major around the place, and whoever else drinks there. (canon) He knows he's been told to write the concert song, and he's seen the Memphis Mafia Bar turned into Humble's "New Graceland." He does not know what he is (the virus in him), and he does not know where Sarah is. (canon/log \'97 secret) The mates know nothing that matters here. [mine]\

\f0\b What's underneath
\f1\b0 \
He's losing his world \'97 the Stickett Inn's a novelty bar full of people he no longer clicks with, and the Memphis Mafia Bar's been taken by the Holy Rollers. The anger in the song is grief he won't say out loud. [mine \'97 from your steer + log \'a7J]\

\f0\b What it pays off and sets up
\f1\b0 \
Pays off: his old drinking-mates and the Stickett Inn \'97 his old life, now changed past him. (canon) Sets up: "Religious Minds," the song the concert will stand on. (log \'a7J) It also shows he writes out of loss, not out of being near Sarah. (log \'a7J)\

\f0\b What must not slip out
\f1\b0 \
Nothing about what Chanta is, the virus, or the effect he has on women. No Sarah, no hint he's writing for her. The song comes from the Holy Rollers and the lost bars, full stop. (log \'97 secret)\

